-- §2  The operations that both draw and induce — the entries `D-transpose N` would have.
#
# ONE ROW PER CROSS-LAYER EDGE: an operation that consumes from one layer while committing on
# another. This is the incidence half of `DᵀN`, which is the half that composes.
#
# ⭐ THE RESULT IS THE FINDING. In this corpus exactly one operation qualifies -- filed twice,
# once in each language -- and its draw is UNMEASURED, so the product cannot be computed at
# all. The matrix that would show cross-layer structure is empty precisely because the
# interesting quantity has no instrument, which is what the model exists to be able to say.
# `d_val` NULL is that.
-- entries/cross_layer_edges.sqlc, the join on the shared (filing, operation) index.
SELECT x.operation        AS "operation!",
       x.drawn_from       AS "drawn!",
       x.drawn::float8    AS d_val,
       x.commits          AS "commits!",
       x.committed::float8 AS n_val
FROM (
    :compose(entries/cross_layer_edges.sqlc)
) x
